ranch="master" change_id="Ie9387fc683ff62a1663034243dafcd21303f33ed" commit="d08e6de0eb5263112488520d5f2ddc25c9e4456f" commit_message="Add write-protect mapping for GD25Q128C  This adds write-protect support for the GD25Q128C.  For future reference, this will probably also work with the GD25Q128B however I was unable to find a datasheet to confirm.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Set WP for lower and upper quadrants and halves using Dediprog programmer, compared raw status value with datasheet.  Change-Id: Ie9387fc683ff62a1663034243dafcd21303f33ed Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332624 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332624" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/24/332624/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie1f60b045a8daacae9f84f7983663d483bfb5d0f" commit="8977b5461d7763640e69b026402a7feba56374f0" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/mediatek: Fix WARN_ON in mtk_drm_crtc_disable().  drm_helper_disable_unused_function doesn't check if the crtc is already disabled before calling the crtc_funcs-&gt;disable(). That then triggers the WARN_ON(), since at boot (mtk_crtc-&gt;enabled == false). We remove the WARN_ON(), let mtk_drm_crtc_disable() silently ignore calls if the crtc is already disabled.  Signed-off-by: Bibby Hsieh &lt;bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50990 TEST=Reboot system on oak-rev5 =&gt; No warning message in mtk_drm_crtc_disable  Change-Id: Ie1f60b045a8daacae9f84f7983663d483bfb5d0f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332320 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bibby Hsieh &lt;bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: CK HU &lt;ck.hu@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="332320" owner_email="bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/332320/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6f4887606e453b2fbc1c53d657e2c9b38238f9fe" commit="bd3e1cbde8382ab08f434e19ea871f273be6cd25" commit_message="site_gtest_runner: Consider tests that didn't finish as failed.  When the gtest process aborts or crashes during a test, the test output will contain the beginning of the test run but not the result so it will remain as 'started' in the gtest_parser. This patch includes the 'started' tests in the the FailedTests() list so tests that abort are reported in the error logs.  BUG=b:27152312 TEST=Nope.  Change-Id: I6f4887606e453b2fbc1c53d657e2c9b38238f9fe Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329768 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="329768" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/68/329768/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If0cf259e30e20a79b7c61776faed79e39c77ab3c" commit="cbbd39c3fc35c7187812924acf1084e0a07152c8" commit_message="UCM config: glados and chell: Set Mic Volume to 24dB  The default value of &quot;Mic Volume&quot; control is 0dB which is too low. This patch sets the gain to +24dB.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51151 TEST=The remote side can hear clearly in hangouts  Change-Id: If0cf259e30e20a79b7c61776faed79e39c77ab3c Signed-off-by: B